IMPORT prelude

-- National Library Board Act 1995 (Singapore) -- what the Act asks of publishers, producers and members of the public: legal deposit
-- of library materials (s 10, with the definitions in s 2), the Board's copying of Singapore websites (s 7(2)(g)), what counts as
-- public archives (s 2), destroying public records (s 17), inspecting them (s 18), reproducing them (s 20), taking them abroad or
-- damaging them (s 21), deposit of recordings on request (s 22), the Board's symbol (s 44), composition (s 45) and the ceiling on
-- penalties in regulations (s 47(2)(j)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition ("incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on
-- 31 December 2021"), informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/NLBA1995.txt. The latest amendment
-- annotated in the text is Act 25 of 2023, in force 1 December 2023 (s 15(3), oaths by live video link), which this row does not
-- encode.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0191 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a
-- sharper question yet. SCOPED to the duties and offences that reach a publisher, a producer of recordings or a member of the public.
-- Not encoded: the Board's constitution, functions and general powers (ss 3-9, 13 and the Schedule), the national union catalogue and
-- interlibrary loans (ss 11, 12, which bind publicly funded libraries), the Director of National Archives and oral history centres
-- (ss 15, 23), the transfers from the Government and the National Heritage Board (ss 24, 25, 36-43), staff and finance (ss 26-35),
-- personal protection (s 46), and anything in the regulations (none was retrieved) -- including the library rules, late-return
-- charges and deposit exemptions that s 47(2) and s 10(2) leave to them.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `National Library Board Act 1995 -- deposit and records`

§§ `2 and 10 -- legal deposit of library materials`

-- s 2: "library materials" covers printed or electronic books, periodicals, newspapers, maps and the like, recorded images and sounds,
-- and "any online material made available on a Singapore website". "published in Singapore", "in relation to library materials
-- OTHER THAN online material, means produced and released in Singapore for sale or public distribution".
-- s 10(1): "Except as otherwise provided by regulations, the publisher of every library material (other than online material)
-- published in Singapore must, at the publisher's own expense -- (a) subject to paragraph (b), deposit 2 copies ... within 4 weeks
-- after the date of first publication; and (b) where the library material is in electronic form, deposit a copy ... free of any
-- technological or other restriction on access, within 4 weeks after the date of first publication."
-- s 10(3): a publisher who contravenes the section is liable to "a fine not exceeding $5,000" (no imprisonment).
-- 4 weeks is taken as 28 days.
DECLARE LibraryMaterial HAS
    `is online material` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is in electronic form` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was produced and released in Singapore for sale or public distribution` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is exempted by regulations` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the material` IS A LibraryMaterial
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the publisher must deposit it` IF
        (NOT `the material`'s `is online material`)
    AND `the material`'s `was produced and released in Singapore for sale or public distribution`
    AND (NOT `the material`'s `is exempted by regulations`)

GIVEN `the material` IS A LibraryMaterial
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of copies to deposit` MEANS
    IF NOT `the publisher must deposit it` `the material` THEN 0
    ELSE IF `the material`'s `is in electronic form` THEN 1
         ELSE 2

GIVEN `the material` IS A LibraryMaterial, `copies deposited` IS A NUMBER, `days after first publication` IS A NUMBER,
      `free of access restrictions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the publisher commits the deposit offence` IF
        `the publisher must deposit it` `the material`
    AND (    `copies deposited` LESS THAN `the number of copies to deposit` `the material`
         OR  `days after first publication` GREATER THAN 28
         OR  (`the material`'s `is in electronic form` AND (NOT `free of access restrictions`)))

§§ `2 and 7(2)(g) -- Singapore websites are copied, not deposited`

-- s 2: "online material" means writing, images, video, sound or data "accessible to the public generally, through the Internet on a
-- website"; "Singapore website" means "(a) any website, the country code top level domain of which is associated with Singapore; or
-- (b) any prescribed website or electronic service associated with Singapore."
-- s 7(2)(g): the Board has power "to make copies of any online material made available on a Singapore website, at the times and in the
-- manner the Board considers appropriate". Nothing in the Act requires the site owner to do anything.
GIVEN `accessible to the public generally` IS A BOOLEAN, `has a Singapore country code domain` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is a prescribed website` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board may copy the online material` IF
        `accessible to the public generally`
    AND (`has a Singapore country code domain` OR `is a prescribed website`)

§§ `2 -- public archives`

-- s 2: "public archives" means those public records that "(a) are more than 25 years old; (b) are specified by the Board as being of
-- national or historical significance; and (c) have been transferred to the Board or to any other place that the Board may determine".
GIVEN `age in years` IS A NUMBER, `specified as of national or historical significance` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `transferred to the Board` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the public records are public archives` IF
        `age in years` GREATER THAN 25
    AND `specified as of national or historical significance`
    AND `transferred to the Board`

§§ `17 -- destroying public records`

-- s 17(1): "A person must not, without the authorisation of the Board under subsection (4), destroy or otherwise dispose of ... any
-- public records which are in the person's possession or under the person's control." (2): the person "must first notify the Board".
-- (3): if the Board requires the records to be made available, "the public records must be made available to the Board". (4): the
-- Board may authorise destruction of classes that "do not in its opinion possess any enduring value".
-- The Act attaches NO penalty to s 17 (regulations under s 47(2)(c) and (j) might; none was read).
GIVEN `notified the Board first` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Board authorised destruction of the class` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Board required the records` IS A BOOLEAN, `made them available` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the destruction complies with s 17` IF
        `notified the Board first`
    AND `the Board authorised destruction of the class`
    AND ((NOT `the Board required the records`) OR `made them available`)

§§ `18 -- inspecting public records and recordings`

-- s 18(1): "Except with the written authority of the Director of National Archives, a person who is not an officer of the National
-- Archives must not inspect any public records or recordings that are not made available to the public under subsection (2)."
-- (2): "Any person may, for the purpose of reference or research, inspect any public archives or recordings made available to the
-- public" subject to the conditions of the originating office or producer and the Director's preservation conditions.
-- No penalty is attached to s 18 in the Act.
GIVEN `is an officer of the National Archives` IS A BOOLEAN, `has the Director's written authority` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `made available to the public` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `inspecting breaches s 18(1)` IF
        (NOT `is an officer of the National Archives`)
    AND (NOT `has the Director's written authority`)
    AND (NOT `made available to the public`)

GIVEN `made available to the public` IS A BOOLEAN, `for reference or research` IS A BOOLEAN, `accepts the conditions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 18(2) entitles the person to inspect` IF
    `made available to the public` AND `for reference or research` AND `accepts the conditions`

§§ `20 -- reproducing public records and recordings`

-- s 20(1): "A person must not publish or reproduce the whole or any part of the contents of any public records which have been
-- transferred to the National Archives or of any recording which has been deposited under section 22 except with the written consent
-- of the Director of National Archives and in accordance with any conditions or restrictions" of the originating office or producer.
-- (2): "a fine not exceeding $5,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or ... both". (3): copyright is unaffected.
DECLARE Item IS ONE OF
    `a public record transferred to the National Archives`
    `a recording deposited under s 22`
    `a public record still held by the public office`
    `a privately owned document`

GIVEN `the item` IS A Item
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 20 covers the item` IF
    CONSIDER `the item`
    WHEN `a public record transferred to the National Archives` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a recording deposited under s 22` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the item` IS A Item, `has the Director's written consent` IS A BOOLEAN, `follows the conditions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reproducing it is an offence under s 20` IF
        `s 20 covers the item` `the item`
    AND ((NOT `has the Director's written consent`) OR (NOT `follows the conditions`))

§§ `21 -- taking public records abroad, defacing or damaging them`

-- s 21(1): "A person must not -- (a) without the written permission of the Board, take or send out of Singapore any public records;
-- (b) write on, mark, inscribe or otherwise deface any public records; or (c) mutilate, excise or otherwise damage any public
-- records." (2): $5,000 or 12 months or both. Only (a) has a permission route; (b) and (c) have none. The section speaks of ANY public
-- records, not only those transferred to the National Archives.
GIVEN `took or sent them out of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `has the Board's written permission` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `defaced them` IS A BOOLEAN, `damaged them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person commits an offence under s 21` IF
        (`took or sent them out of Singapore` AND (NOT `has the Board's written permission`))
    OR  `defaced them`
    OR  `damaged them`

§§ `22 -- recordings on request`

-- s 22(1): "The producer or distributor of a recording must, within 6 months after a request in writing is made by the Board, provide
-- (without charge) the Board with a copy of the recording". (2): $5,000 or 12 months or both. (3): not for "(a) a recording that has
-- not been broadcast or made public in Singapore" or (b) an exempted class. (4): "recording" means "anything in which sounds are
-- embodied or on which images are fixed or both, regardless of form".
GIVEN `the Board requested it in writing` IS A BOOLEAN, `broadcast or made public in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `of an exempted class` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the producer must provide a copy` IF
        `the Board requested it in writing`
    AND `broadcast or made public in Singapore`
    AND (NOT `of an exempted class`)

GIVEN `the Board requested it in writing` IS A BOOLEAN, `broadcast or made public in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `of an exempted class` IS A BOOLEAN, `provided a copy` IS A BOOLEAN, `months after the request` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the producer commits an offence under s 22` IF
        `the producer must provide a copy` `the Board requested it in writing` `broadcast or made public in Singapore` `of an exempted class`
    AND ((NOT `provided a copy`) OR `months after the request` GREATER THAN 6)

§§ `44 -- the Board's symbol`

-- s 44(2): "A person who, without the permission of the Board, uses a symbol or representation identical with that of the Board or
-- which so resembles the Board's symbol or representation as to deceive or cause confusion, or to be likely to deceive or cause
-- confusion" -- $5,000 or 6 months or both.
GIVEN `has the Board's permission` IS A BOOLEAN, `identical to the Board's symbol` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `likely to deceive or cause confusion` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `using the symbol is an offence under s 44` IF
        (NOT `has the Board's permission`)
    AND (`identical to the Board's symbol` OR `likely to deceive or cause confusion`)

§§ `10(3), 20(2), 21(2), 22(2), 44(2), 47(2)(j) -- maximum penalties`

-- Every offence in the Act carries a fine of up to $5,000; regulations may create offences but "which penalties shall not exceed a fine
-- of $5,000" (s 47(2)(j)). Imprisonment: none for s 10 or regulations; 12 months for ss 20, 21, 22; 6 months for s 44.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `failing to deposit library material`
    `reproducing archives without consent`
    `taking abroad or damaging public records`
    `failing to provide a recording`
    `misusing the Board's symbol`
    `breaching the Board's regulations`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS 5000

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `reproducing archives without consent` THEN 12
    WHEN `taking abroad or damaging public records` THEN 12
    WHEN `failing to provide a recording` THEN 12
    WHEN `misusing the Board's symbol` THEN 6
    OTHERWISE 0

§§ `45 -- composition`

-- s 45(1): the chief executive officer or an authorised officer "may compound any offence under this Act that is prescribed as a
-- compoundable offence by collecting ... a sum not exceeding $500". (2): on payment, "no further proceedings are to be taken".
-- Which offences are prescribed is in regulations, not read.
GIVEN `prescribed as compoundable` IS A BOOLEAN, `sum` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence may be compounded for the sum` IF
    `prescribed as compoundable` AND `sum` AT MOST 500
